    "text": "Done! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack in Cuis with comprehensive tests. Here's what was created:\n\n**BoundedStack class** (category 'BoundedStack'):\n- `new: aCapacity` - creates a stack with specified capacity\n- `initializeWithCapacity:` - validates capacity is a positive integer (fails with \"capacity must be a positive integer\" otherwise)\n- `push:` - adds an object; fails with \"stack is full\" when at capacity\n- `pop` - removes and returns the top object; fails with \"stack is empty\" when empty\n- `top` - returns the top object without removing it; fails with \"stack is empty\" when empty\n- `isEmpty` - returns whether the stack is empty\n- `size` - returns the current number of elements\n\n**BoundedStackTest** (category 'BoundedStack-Tests'):\nAll 14 tests pass:\n- Capacity validation (valid, zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Basic push/pop operations\n- Top method (returns without removing)\n- Multiple push/pop operations (LIFO behavior)\n- Full stack error handling\n- Empty stack error handling (pop and top)\n- Stack reuse after emptying\n- Multiple object types (integers, strings, symbols, arrays)\n- Size tracking throughout operations\n- Filling stack to capacity\n\nThe image has been saved with all changes."
